L176:   * Blame\nL177: \nL178: 80 lines (61 loc) · 5.32 KB\nL179: \nL180: 【70†Raw】\nL181: \nL182: Copy raw file\nL183: \nL184: Download raw file\nL185: \nL186: Outline\nL187: \nL188: Edit and raw actions\nL189: \nL190: # Changelog\nL191: \nL192: All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\nL193: \nL194: ## [Unreleased] — Canonical Rewrite\nL195: \nL196: Major revision: unified API, one verifier, one proof type, 7 provers, SIMD acceleration.\nL197: ### Breaking\nL198:   * Package renamed from `efficient-sumcheck` to `effsc`.\nL199:   * Single verifier — `sumcheck_verify()` returns `SumcheckResult { challenges, final_claim }`. The oracle check is the caller's responsibility (【71†Thaler Remark 4.2†people.cs.georgetown.edu】). Removed `inner_product_sumcheck_verify`, `multilinear_sumcheck_verify`, and `coefficient_sumcheck::sumcheck_verify`.\nL200:   * Single proof type — `SumcheckProof<F>` replaces `Sumcheck<F>` and `ProductSumcheck<F>`.\nL201:   * Transcript redesigned — `send()`/`receive()`/`challenge()` replace `read()`/`write()`.\nL202:   * Legacy entry points demoted — use `runner::sumcheck()` with a prover type.\nL203:   * Wire format: EvalsInfty. `d` values per round instead of `d + 1`; consistency is now structural. Details in 【72†docs/design.md §7a】.\nL204: ### Added\nL205:   * `SumcheckProver<F>` trait — single extension point for all polynomial shapes.\nL206:   * 7 concrete provers — `MultilinearProver`, `InnerProductProver`, `CoefficientProver` (each with MSB + LSB variants), `GkrProver`.\nL207:   * `SumcheckField` trait — generic field interface; blanket impl for `ark_ff::Field` behind `feature = \"arkworks\"`.\nL208:   * `SimdRepr` trait — safe SIMD opt-in with `zerocopy` layout verification.\nL209:   * `runner::sumcheck()` — single runner with partial execution and per-round hooks.\nL210:   * Eq polynomial utilities — `eq_poly`, `eq_poly_non_binary`, O(2^v) incremental `compute_hypercube_eq_evals`.\nL211:   * Adversarial verifier tests — corrupted proofs, wrong sums, wrong final values across all prover types.\nL212:   * `no_std` support — core library works without `arkworks` feature.\nL213:   * SIMD — transparent 8-wide AVX-512 IFMA, 2-wide NEON acceleration.\nL214: ### Integrations\nL215: \nL216:   * 【73†WHIR】 (【74†PR #250】)\nL217:   * 【75†WARP】 (【76†PR #24】)\nL218: \nL219: ### Removed\nL220: \nL221:   * ~4,500 lines of legacy code — old `Prover` trait, `TimeProver`/`SpaceProver`/`BlendyProver`, `OrderStrategy`, `messages/`, `interpolation/`, `simd_ops`.\nL222: \nL223: ## [0.0.2] - 2026-02-11\nL224: ### Added\nL225:   * High-level API: `multilinear_sumcheck()` and `inner_product_sumcheck()` free functions for simple one-call sumcheck.\nL226:   * Fiat–Shamir support: `Transcript` trait with `SpongefishTranscript` (real Fiat-Shamir via 【77†SpongeFish】) and `SanityTranscript` (random challenges for testing).\nL227:   * `batched_constraint_poly` — merges dense and sparse polynomials into a single constraint polynomial.\nL228:   * Pairwise reduce for `TimeProductProver` (【78†#87】).\nL229:   * Improved order strategies (【79†#86】).\nL230:   * Pairwise compression for `TimeProver` (【80†#83】).\nL231:   * `BasicProver` for testing (【81†#84】).\nL232: ### Changed\nL233: \nL234:   * Removed `claim` from the `Prover` trait (【82†#85】).\nL235:   * Updated to criterion 0.8 (【83†#88】).\nL236: \nL237: ## [0.0.1] - 2025-08-26\nL238: ### Added\nL239: \nL240:   * Rayon parallelization for `TimeProver` and `TimeProductProver` (【84†#80】).\nL241:   * Stream iterator for sequential evaluation access (【85†#74】).\nL242:   * Benchmark improvements (【86†#75】, 【87†#76】).\nL243:   * `FileStream` for memory-mapped file-backed evaluations (【88†#67】).\nL244:   * Blendy product prover — `BlendyProductProver` (【89†#64】).\nL245:   * Refactored module structure (【90†#63】).\nL246: ### Changed\nL247: \nL248:   * Bumped arkworks dependencies from 0.4 → 0.5.\nL249:   * Avoid dynamic dispatch (`dyn`) and heap allocation (`Box`) (【91†#53】).\nL250:   * Gray code ordering for sequential Lagrange polynomial iterator (【92†#55】).\nL251: \nL252: ## [0.0.0] - 2024-02-09\nL253: ### Added\nL254:   * Initial release with three proving algorithms:\nL255:     * `SpaceProver` — quasi-linear time, logarithmic space [【93†CTY11†arxiv.org】].\nL256:     * `TimeProver` — linear time, linear space [【94†VSBW13†ieeexplore.ieee.org】].\nL257:     * `BlendyProver` — linear time, sublinear space [【95†CFFZ24†eprint.iacr.org】].\nL258:   * Product sumcheck variants (`SpaceProductProver`, `TimeProductProver`, `BlendyProductProver`).\nL259:   * `MemoryStream` for in-memory evaluation access.\nL260:   * Hypercube utilities and Lagrange polynomial interpolation.\nL261:   * Configurable reduction modes (pairwise, variablewise).\nL262:   * Benchmark suite using criterion.\nL263: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n"
